      {
        "type": "thinking",
        "thinking": "I'm working through the root स्मि (smi), ātmanepada and aniṭ, trying to derive its luṅ (aorist) third person plural form by building up aṭ + stem + sic + jha and checking whether guṇa applies in the ātmanepada sic formation.\n\nApplying 1.2.11 (लिङ्सिचावात्मनेपदेषु), since स्मि ends in a vowel rather than a consonant, the sic here is not kit, so guṇa applies and I get अस्मेष्ट with the bahuvacana jha becoming अत् by 7.1.5, yielding अस्मेषत — with ṣatva applying since the sibilant follows इ.\n\n",
